  "summary": [
   "This 1960s ranch house in North Dallas had a closed-off floor plan that the client wanted to open up. Three load-bearing walls were removed, and four new LVL beams were set into the attic to carry the roof load. The result is one continuous kitchen, living and dining area, with natural light and sight lines running from the front of the house to the back.",
   "The details carry the same care. A quartzite-wrapped range hood anchors the kitchen. At the entry, a lit step resolves an existing change in level and marks the transition from the shared living spaces to the private bedroom wing. Custom pendant and sconce lighting completes the scheme."
  ],
